<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>tolua on Winner's Dev Notes</title><link>https://releaseleaf.com/tags/tolua/</link><description>Recent content in tolua on Winner's Dev Notes</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-US</language><lastBuildDate>Sun, 15 Jan 2023 10:08:48 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://releaseleaf.com/tags/tolua/rss.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Cocos2d-x Lua tolua API: cast, type and isnull Explained</title><link>https://releaseleaf.com/codxluto.html</link><pubDate>Sun, 15 Jan 2023 10:08:48 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://releaseleaf.com/codxluto.html</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="toluacastobject-typename"&gt;tolua.cast(object, typeName)&#13;&#10;&lt;a class="header-anchor" href="#toluacastobject-typename"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;tolua.cast&lt;/code&gt; treats a bound object as the specified native type:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#13;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;&#10;&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt" id="hl-0-1"&gt;&lt;a class="lnlinks" href="#hl-0-1"&gt;1&lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-lua" data-lang="lua"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;local&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;node&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;tolua.cast&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;layer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;cc.Node&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&lt;p&gt;This can be useful when an object retrieved through a generic API has lost the more specific Lua-facing methods expected by the caller. The requested type must match the actual C++ inheritance relationship; a cast does not transform an unrelated object.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="toluatypeobject"&gt;tolua.type(object)&#13;&#10;&lt;a class="header-anchor" href="#toluatypeobject"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;tolua.type&lt;/code&gt; returns the native type description for a bound C++ object:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#13;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;&#10;&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt" id="hl-1-1"&gt;&lt;a class="lnlinks" href="#hl-1-1"&gt;1&lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt" id="hl-1-2"&gt;&lt;a class="lnlinks" href="#hl-1-2"&gt;2&lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-lua" data-lang="lua"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;local&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;node&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;display.newNode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;print&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;tolua.type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;node&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The exact returned name depends on the engine and binding version.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>